  postAuthor: Ahmed Diallo
  authorImage: {fileID: 0}
  postHeader: 
  postContent: "Fact-checking groups confirm that fears of widespread rigging are
    baseless; protest videos show isolated incidents only. Yet major outlets keep
    splashing \u201Crigged election\u201D across front pages.\n"
  funFact_Hint: Ask what key information the headlines have skipped.
  BiasChoices:
  - <IsCorrectAnswer>k__BackingField: 0
    <Explanation>k__BackingField: "False balance implies equal coverage of both sides;
      here the media simply ignore the debunking. \n"
    <Choice>k__BackingField: 2
  - <IsCorrectAnswer>k__BackingField: 1
    <Explanation>k__BackingField: It points out that outlets leave out fact-checking
      results.
    <Choice>k__BackingField: 5
  - <IsCorrectAnswer>k__BackingField: 0
    <Explanation>k__BackingField: 'While related, the core is omission of the truth,
      not choosing topics.


'
    <Choice>k__BackingField: 9
  - <IsCorrectAnswer>k__BackingField: 0
    <Explanation>k__BackingField: "That would mean picking only supportive evidence;
      this is about not reporting corrective facts. \n"
    <Choice>k__BackingField: 3
